.TH ORO-CHILD_PROCESS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:child_process \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:child_process'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
oro:child_process is a JavaScript API module exposed by the Oro Runtime.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBPipe (extends AsyncResource)\fR
This is an exported `ClassDeclaration` named ``Pipe` (extends `AsyncResource`)`, but it does not yet have a dedicated description in the generated reference.
.TP
\fBreading()\fR
`true` if the pipe is still reading, otherwise `false`.
.TP
\fBprocess()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBdestroy()\fR
Destroys the pipe
.TP
\fBChildProcess (extends EventEmitter)\fR
This is an exported `ClassDeclaration` named ``ChildProcess` (extends `EventEmitter`)`, but it does not yet have a dedicated description in the generated reference.
.TP
\fBconstructor(options)\fR
`ChildProcess` class constructor.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ChildProcessOptions; optional; default null)
.TP
\fBkilled()\fR
`true` if the child process was killed with kill()`, otherwise `false`.
.TP
\fBpid()\fR
The process identifier for the child process. This value is `> 0` if the process was spawned successfully, otherwise `0`.
.TP
\fBspawnfile()\fR
The executable file name of the child process that is launched. This value is `null` until the child process has successfully been spawned.
.TP
\fBspawnargs()\fR
The full list of command\-line arguments the child process was spawned with. This value is an empty array until the child process has successfully been spawned.
.TP
\fBconnected()\fR
Always `false` as the IPC messaging is not supported.
.TP
\fBexitCode()\fR
The child process exit code. This value is `null` if the child process is still running, otherwise it is a positive integer.
.TP
\fBstdin()\fR
If available, the underlying `stdin` writable stream for the child process.
.TP
\fBstdout()\fR
If available, the underlying `stdout` readable stream for the child process.
.TP
\fBstderr()\fR
If available, the underlying `stderr` readable stream for the child process.
.TP
\fBdisconnect()\fR
This function does nothing, but is present for nodejs compat.
.TP
\fBsend()\fR
This function does nothing, but is present for nodejs compat.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBref()\fR
This function does nothing, but is present for nodejs compat.
.TP
\fBunref()\fR
This function does nothing, but is present for nodejs compat.
.TP
\fBkill(signal)\fR
Kills the child process. This function throws an error if the child process has not been spawned or is already killed.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIsignal\fR (number \\| string; required)
.TP
\fBspawn(command, args, options)\fR
Spawns the child process. This function will throw an error if the process is already spawned.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIcommand\fR (string; required) Executable name or path.
.br
\fIargs\fR (string[] \\| ChildProcessOptions; optional) Tokenized arguments or options.
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ChildProcessOptions; optional; default null) Spawn options.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIChildProcess\fR
.TP
\fBaddEventListener(event, callback, options)\fR
`EventTarget` based `addEventListener` method.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIevent\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function(Event); required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ once?: false }; optional; default null)
.TP
